<p>Build and deploy a product-manual assistant: upload text, index it, then ask questions with cited answers. All application code is supplied.</p>
<h2 id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Azure:</strong> an active subscription, resource/role-assignment permissions, and model/VM quota.</li><li><strong>Local:</strong> Azure CLI, Bicep, Docker, kubectl, Java 21, Python 3.12+ and Git. On Windows, use Ubuntu in WSL2 with Docker Desktop integration.</li></ul>
<p>Use the <a href="./prerequisites.html#before-you-begin">prerequisite checklist</a> and <a href="./prerequisites.html#windows-setup">setup downloads</a>. Allow about four hours <em>after</em> setup; this estimate has not been timed.</p>
<h2 id="finished">The three applications</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Products</td><td>Java 21 / Spring Boot on AKS. Server-rendered upload/chat UI; JDBC, PostgreSQL and Flyway. Always at least one replica.</td></tr><tr><td>ProductsEmbedder</td><td>Python Function. Reads uploaded manuals, creates chunks/embeddings and stores them in pgvector.</td></tr><tr><td>ProductsChat</td><td>Python worker on AKS. Retrieves chunks, calls the chat model and replies through Service Bus. KEDA scales it from zero.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<details class="optional" id="upload-flow"><summary>Upload and indexing flow</summary>
<figure class="flow" aria-label="Upload and indexing architecture"><div class="flow-node"><strong>Products</strong>Commit product + manual ID</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Private blob</strong>Upload .txt</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Event Grid → Function</strong>Read, chunk, embed</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>PostgreSQL</strong>Store vectors; mark ready</div><figcaption>Upload success precedes indexing completion. Event Grid carries a notification; the Function reads the blob separately.</figcaption></figure>
</details>
<details class="optional" id="question-flow"><summary>Question and answer flow</summary>
<figure class="flow" aria-label="Asynchronous RAG architecture"><div class="flow-node"><strong>Products + DB</strong>Persist question + outbox</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Request queue</strong>Service Bus</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Chat worker</strong>Embed → retrieve → generate</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Reply queue → Products</strong>Persist answer; browser polls</div><figcaption>Persistent request/correlation IDs connect the flow. Embeddings find evidence; the LLM generates the answer.</figcaption></figure>
</details>
<p>Selected <a href="./reference.html#exam">AI-200 objectives</a>. Use the shared term tooltips for definitions; <a href="./reference.html">reference notes</a> cover costs and design tradeoffs.</p>
